From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:56:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: sun6i-dma: Use bit 0 to pause an A733 channel

The A733 pauses a channel with bit 0 of its DMA_PAU_REG; bits 31:1 are
reserved (A733 user manual, section 13.1.7.7). The driver writes bit 1,
the pause bit of the older controllers. On the A733 that write is
dropped and the register reads back 0, so dmaengine_pause() reports
success while the transfer goes on.

Add the pause bit to the per-SoC configuration and set bit 0 for the
A733. The other SoCs leave it at 0 and keep writing bit 1. Resume
writes 0 to the register and needs no change.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; sun6i-dma probes and
dmatest passes with this change. The pause path is not exercised: no
client in this test pauses a channel.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/dma/sun6i-dma.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/sun6i-dma.c b/drivers/dma/sun6i-dma.c
index db4946947b5b..d2c612a05ef9 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/sun6i-dma.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/sun6i-dma.c
@@ -72,6 +72,7 @@
 
 #define DMA_CHAN_PAUSE		0x04
 #define DMA_CHAN_PAUSE_PAUSE		BIT(1)
+#define DMA_CHAN_PAUSE_PAUSE_A733	BIT(0)
 #define DMA_CHAN_PAUSE_RESUME		0
 
 #define DMA_CHAN_LLI_ADDR	0x08
@@ -162,6 +163,8 @@ struct sun6i_dma_config {
 	u32 irq_en_offset;
 	u32 irq_stat_offset;
 	u32 num_channels_per_reg;
+	/* Pause bit of DMA_CHAN_PAUSE, 0 means DMA_CHAN_PAUSE_PAUSE */
+	u32 pause_bit;
 };
 
 /*
@@ -941,7 +944,7 @@ static int sun6i_dma_pause(struct dma_chan *chan)
 	dev_dbg(chan2dev(chan), "vchan %p: pause\n", &vchan->vc);
 
 	if (pchan) {
-		writel(DMA_CHAN_PAUSE_PAUSE,
+		writel(sdev->cfg->pause_bit ?: DMA_CHAN_PAUSE_PAUSE,
 		       pchan->base + DMA_CHAN_PAUSE);
 	} else {
 		spin_lock(&sdev->lock);
@@ -1350,6 +1353,7 @@ static struct sun6i_dma_config sun60i_a733_dma_cfg = {
 	.irq_en_offset   = DMA_IRQ_EN_OFFSET_A733,
 	.irq_stat_offset = DMA_IRQ_STAT_OFFSET_A733,
 	.num_channels_per_reg = DMA_IRQ_CHAN_NR_A733,
+	.pause_bit = DMA_CHAN_PAUSE_PAUSE_A733,
 };
 
 /*
